# web-ping.sh targets. Copy to targets.conf (which git ignores) and edit,
# or let ./add-target.sh create and maintain it for you.
#
# Format: URL | MAX_HOPS | COOKIE_PATH | EXPECTED_TEXT | FINAL_URL
#
#   URL            Page to fetch. Redirects are followed.
#   MAX_HOPS       Most redirects allowed. Use the count from a logged-in
#                  `./web-ping.sh --trace` run; 0 if the URL loads directly.
#                  A strict limit makes an expired cookie (which redirects to
#                  a login page) fail instead of passing.
#   COOKIE_PATH    Netscape-format cookie file for sites that need a login,
#                  or '-' for none. Create it with ./add-target.sh. Paths are
#                  relative to the directory web-ping.sh is run from.
#   EXPECTED_TEXT  Text the response must contain (blank = anything). Take it
#                  from what curl receives, not what the browser shows, and
#                  pick something only present when logged in. Start it with
#                  '~' to ignore upper/lower case: ~sign out
#                  (to match a literal leading '~' with case, write '\~').
#                  Values in any field cannot contain '|'.
#   FINAL_URL      Optional. Checks the URL of the page you end up on after
#                  the redirects. Space-separated terms, ignoring case: each
#                  must appear in that URL; a term starting with '!' must NOT.
#                  It catches being sent somewhere other than intended, such
#                  as a maintenance page during patching, a sign-in page when
#                  a session expires, or an error page, even when that page
#                  returns 200 and shares text (like a site footer) with the
#                  real one. Example: "app.example.com/home !maintenance".
#                  Leave the field off, or use '-', to skip the check.
#
# Lines starting with '#' and blank lines are ignored.

# Public page, no login, must load without redirects
https://www.example.com/|0|-|Example Domain

# Page behind a login: one expected redirect, text only shown when signed in
# (any case), and it must end on the app's home page, not a login page
https://app.example.com/|1|./cookies/app.example.com|~sign out|app.example.com/home !login
